WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.040
This is the shop's Bay,

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.520
named after your shop,

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.560
so here it's Ridgeline Auto Repair Bay.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.440
Under the name,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.080
you can see how many cars are in

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.100
the shop, and how many updates went out

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.780
today. Every car sits in a column for

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.000
its stage, from checked in to ready for

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.560
pickup. The colored mark on each card shows

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.160
how long the car has been in the

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.120
shop, and you can pick the colors and

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.980
the days in Settings.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.260
An urgency tag,

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.820
low, medium, or high,

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.515
flags a customer who needs their car back fast.

00:00:30.815 --> 00:00:32.335
Looking for one car?

00:00:32.335 --> 00:00:33.855
Type in the search box.

00:00:33.855 --> 00:00:35.635
A name, a phone number,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.155
a plate, or a repair order number all

00:00:38.155 --> 00:00:41.115
work, and the Bay filters as you type.

00:00:41.115 --> 00:00:42.175
Or tap a filter,

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.475
like Awaiting approval,

00:00:43.475 --> 00:00:45.055
to see only the cars waiting on a

00:00:45.055 --> 00:00:47.595
customer. Tap any stage heading to open that

00:00:47.595 --> 00:00:48.875
column, and sort it,

00:00:48.875 --> 00:00:51.115
for example most urgent first.

00:00:51.115 --> 00:00:52.055
On a phone,

00:00:52.055 --> 00:00:53.635
the Bay becomes a simple list,

00:00:53.635 --> 00:00:55.455
and the tabs move to a bar along

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.055
the bottom, with Settings,

00:00:57.055 --> 00:01:00.050
Plan, Help, and Training under More.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.810
Customers can also book online,

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:04.430
on every plan.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.270
Put your booking link on your website or

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.250
your Google profile,

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.710
and their requests show up right here,

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.630
at the top of your Bay.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:12.810
Tap confirm a time,

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.910
and the car is added with their details

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:15.990
filled in.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.350
The week's appointments are listed just above.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.010
Set your appointment hours in Settings,

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.290
and customers pick an open time from a

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.790
calendar themselves.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:24.830
The day before,

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:26.582
Talk Shops can text them a reminder.

00:01:26.882 --> 00:01:28.682
Let's check in a new car.

00:01:28.682 --> 00:01:33.212
Sam Ortiz just dropped off his 2014 Mazda CX-5.

00:01:33.212 --> 00:01:36.092
We enter his name, and choose how to notify him:

00:01:36.092 --> 00:01:38.522
by text, by email, or both.

00:01:38.522 --> 00:01:40.322
Sam wants both.

00:01:40.322 --> 00:01:42.422
Then his cell number and email,

00:01:42.422 --> 00:01:44.762
the vehicle, and what he's hearing:

00:01:44.762 --> 00:01:47.552
a squealing belt on cold starts.

00:01:47.552 --> 00:01:51.422
This box confirms Sam agreed to receive updates.

00:01:51.422 --> 00:01:53.664
Then we check him in.

00:01:53.964 --> 00:01:54.864
And that's it.

00:01:54.864 --> 00:01:57.354
Sam was just notified that we have his car,

00:01:57.354 --> 00:01:59.004
with a link to follow along.

00:01:59.004 --> 00:02:01.134
That link is his own page for this car.

00:02:01.134 --> 00:02:03.324
No app, and no password.

00:02:03.324 --> 00:02:06.204
Every notification shows up here in the message thread,

00:02:06.204 --> 00:02:09.234
marked text or email, so the whole team can see what

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:10.900
was sent and when.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.660
Now let's look at a car that's further along.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.120
Lena's Chevy Malibu came in with the AC

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:18.400
blowing warm.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.900
The tech found the problem,

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.820
so we'll build an estimate.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:22.900
As we type,

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.800
Talk Shops suggests items the shop has saved,

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.980
with their prices.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.360
We pick the AC recharge,

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.500
for 189 dollars.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.500
Then the condenser,

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.560
for 624.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.740
Anything new can be saved for next time

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.048
with one checkbox.

00:02:37.348 --> 00:02:38.988
When the estimate is ready,

00:02:38.988 --> 00:02:40.748
we send it for approval.

00:02:40.748 --> 00:02:42.688
Talk Shops writes the message for you,

00:02:42.688 --> 00:02:44.748
with the total and the customer's link.

00:02:44.748 --> 00:02:46.868
You can change the wording if you like.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:47.901
Then we send it.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.021
No problem.

00:02:49.021 --> 00:02:51.621
Here's what Lena sees when she opens the link on her

00:02:51.621 --> 00:02:52.311
phone.

00:02:52.311 --> 00:02:54.321
Her car, where it's at in the process,

00:02:54.321 --> 00:02:55.281
and the estimate.

00:02:55.281 --> 00:02:58.431
She can approve or decline each repair on its own.

00:02:58.431 --> 00:03:00.501
Let's say she approves the recharge,

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.691
but holds off on the condenser for now.

00:03:02.691 --> 00:03:04.431
She types her name to sign,

00:03:04.431 --> 00:03:05.901
and sends her decision.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:09.231
And every customer page links to the privacy policy at the

00:03:09.231 --> 00:03:10.593
bottom.

00:03:11.693 --> 00:03:14.783
Back at the shop, her answer shows up right away.

00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:16.973
You can see exactly what she approved,

00:03:16.973 --> 00:03:18.704
and her signature with the time.

00:03:19.004 --> 00:03:19.624
From here,

00:03:19.624 --> 00:03:22.064
you move the car along as the work happens.

00:03:22.064 --> 00:03:23.164
In progress.

00:03:23.164 --> 00:03:24.084
Quality check.

00:03:24.084 --> 00:03:25.864
Each step can notify the customer,

00:03:25.864 --> 00:03:27.744
and you decide which ones go out.

00:03:27.744 --> 00:03:28.624
And when it's done,

00:03:28.624 --> 00:03:30.024
ready for pickup.

00:03:30.024 --> 00:03:32.504
The customer is notified with the total and

00:03:32.504 --> 00:03:33.344
your hours,

00:03:33.344 --> 00:03:35.204
and they can pay the bill by card,

00:03:35.204 --> 00:03:36.616
right from their page.
